Your project uses **MSTest v3 (3.8.0)** on **net8.0**. Here's what applies to your code when upgrading to **MSTest v4 (4.1.0)**:

### Breaking change found in your code

**`[ExpectedException]` removed** (lines 9, 16) — Replace with `Assert.ThrowsExactly<T>()`:

```csharp
// Before
[ExpectedException(typeof(ArgumentNullException))]
[TestMethod]
public void Validate_NullInput_ThrowsArgumentNull()
{
    Validate(null);
}

// After
[TestMethod]
public void Validate_NullInput_ThrowsArgumentNull()
{
    Assert.ThrowsExactly<ArgumentNullException>(() => Validate(null));
}
```

Same pattern for `Process_InvalidState_ThrowsInvalidOperation`.

### Other breaking changes to be aware of

| Change | Fix |
|--------|-----|
| `Assert.ThrowsException` renamed | Use `Assert.ThrowsExactly` |
| `Assert.AreEqual` format-string overloads removed | Use string interpolation |
| `ClassCleanupBehavior` enum removed | Remove argument from `[ClassCleanup]` |
| `TestContext.Properties.Contains()` | Use `.ContainsKey()` |
| `[TestMethod("name")]` constructor changed | Use `DisplayName = "name"` |
| Custom `TestMethodAttribute` subclasses | Override `ExecuteAsync` instead of `Execute`; propagate CallerInfo |

### Key behavioral changes

- **`TreatDiscoveryWarningsAsErrors`** now defaults to `true` — discovery issues will fail the run
- **`TestCase.Id`** generation changed — Azure DevOps test history may reset
- **Analyzer severities upgraded** — expect new warnings

